RPC-test by smiler of teso

This a simple interface to the RPC protocol designed to make it easy to 
'exercise' any service running on top of RPC by sending arbitrary strings, 
integers and opaque data etc. it is also a handy way of using pmap_dump over 
udp :>

If you don't know anything about the RPC or XDR protocol I suggest you read 
the RFCs before you try this...

try typing 'help' at any point if you don't know the usage, or even 
better read the source :>

Note I've only really tryed this on linux (well actually only rpc.mountd ;).

If you can't think of a use for this program cast your minds back a year or so 
when the rpc.mountd vulnerability was first reported. It was really quite a 
simple bug, just attempt to mount a rather long directory and boom, a stack 
overflow.  Probably the only reason it wasnt discovered earlier was that it 
was buried beneath the rpc protocol which is pretty inaccessible from the 
command line (and the C API is shite too). Hopefully rpctest will make it
easier to findbugs of this kind...

-smiler
